        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "24c4636a-8f45-520e-ba5b-5fb789790330",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mesih Pasha, Constantine XI Palaiologos\n- Roles: Ottoman statesman, Byzantine emperor\n- Places: Constantinople\n- Organizations: Palaiologos dynasty\n\nFacts:\n- Constantine XI Palaiologos was born on 8 February 1405.\n- Constantine XI Palaiologos was the last reigning Byzantine Emperor and a member of the Palaiologos dynasty.\n- Constantine XI Palaiologos reigned from 1449 until his death in battle at the fall of Constantinople on 29 May 1453.\n- Mesih Pasha was an Ottoman statesman of Byzantine Greek origin.\n- Mesih Pasha was a nephew of Constantine XI Palaiologos, the last Byzantine emperor.\n- Mesih Pasha, also called Misac Pasha, died in November 1501.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
